From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] nfc: nci: map the Frame RF protocols explicitly

The NCI specification says protocols without an RF_DISCOVER_MAP entry
default to the Frame RF interface, but NXP NCI 2.0 controllers such as
the SN100x require the mapping to be present. Without explicit T1T,
T2T, T3T and T5T Frame mappings, RF discovery reports success but no tag
ever activates.

Map the four Frame protocols in nci_init_complete_req() before the
ISO-DEP and NFC-DEP entries, with the same NCI_MAX_NUM_MAPPING_CONFIGS
guard the loop already uses. Only do it for controllers that report NCI
2.0: NCI 1.x does not define T5T (protocol 0x06), and a 1.x controller
could reject the whole RF_DISCOVER_MAP, so their map stays as before.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 net/nfc/nci/core.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/nfc/nci/core.c b/net/nfc/nci/core.c
--- a/net/nfc/nci/core.c
+++ b/net/nfc/nci/core.c
@@ -187,6 +187,30 @@ static void nci_init_complete_req(struct nci_dev *ndev, const void *opt)
 	/* set rf mapping configurations */
 	*num = 0;
 
+	/*
+	 * Explicitly map T1T, T2T, T3T and T5T to the Frame RF interface on
+	 * NCI 2.0 controllers. The specification says unmapped protocols
+	 * default to Frame RF, but NXP NCI 2.0 controllers such as the SN100x
+	 * require the mapping to be explicit or tag discovery yields no
+	 * notifications. NCI 1.x does not define T5T (protocol 0x06), so a
+	 * 1.x controller could reject the whole RF_DISCOVER_MAP; leave those
+	 * as they were.
+	 */
+	if (ndev->nci_ver & NCI_VER_2_MASK) {
+		static const u8 frame_protocols[] = {
+			NCI_RF_PROTOCOL_T1T, NCI_RF_PROTOCOL_T2T,
+			NCI_RF_PROTOCOL_T3T, NCI_RF_PROTOCOL_T5T,
+		};
+
+		for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(frame_protocols) &&
+			    *num < NCI_MAX_NUM_MAPPING_CONFIGS; i++) {
+			cfg[*num].rf_protocol = frame_protocols[i];
+			cfg[*num].mode = NCI_DISC_MAP_MODE_POLL;
+			cfg[*num].rf_interface = NCI_RF_INTERFACE_FRAME;
+			(*num)++;
+		}
+	}
+
 	/* by default mapping is set to NCI_RF_INTERFACE_FRAME */
 	for (i = 0; i < ndev->num_supported_rf_interfaces; i++) {
 		if (ndev->supported_rf_interfaces[i] ==
